WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.190
Here's a game.

2
00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.530
One part of the program adds
up your score as you play.

3
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.390
Another part adds up the cost of
everything in your shop basket.

4
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.410
Both parts use a variable called total.

5
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.450
Yet the score never gets
mixed up with the bill.

6
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.970
Shouldn't one total overwrite the other?

7
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.190
So why is there no clash?

8
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.690
In this mission, you'll learn that a
subroutine is a named block of code.

9
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.290
It runs when you call it by its name.

10
00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:30.910
You'll pass data in with parameters, and
see a function send its result back with

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.070
return.

12
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.210
Your mission: explain why two subroutines
can both use a variable called total

13
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.320
without a clash.
